---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  StateSamplePlayground,
  StateSampleGallery,
  StateSampleWindows,
  StateSampleParts,
} from "../../components/StateSampleDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="State Sample"
  description="Small, decorative pictures of a filled page for empty states."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">State Sample</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Draws a small picture of a page once it has content. Pass it to an empty <a
      href="/components/state-panel/">State Panel</a
    > so people see what they will get before they add anything.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><StateSamplePlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="State sample usage"
      code={`import {
  SampleIconTile,
  SampleList,
  SampleText,
  SampleWindow,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/state-sample";

<StatePanel
  kind="empty"
  icon={ChatRound}
  title="No chats yet"
  description="Every private conversation is saved here."
  sample={
    <SampleWindow icon={ChatRound} trail={["Chats"]} tabs={["Active", "Archived"]}>
      <SampleList
        items={[
          {
            leading: <SampleIconTile icon={ChatRound} />,
            title: "Draft a follow-up for Northwind",
            detail: "Draft ready for your review",
            trailing: <SampleText tone="muted">1h ago</SampleText>,
          },
        ]}
      />
    </SampleWindow>
  }
>
  <Button>Start a chat</Button>
</StatePanel>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>SampleWindow</code> draws a title bar with <code>icon</code>, a
      breadcrumb <code>trail</code>, and an “Example” chip. Change the chip with <code
        >label</code
      >. The last trail part is the current page. Add <code>tabs</code> for a tab
      row; the first tab is selected. Put a list, a table, or your own content inside.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Every sample</h2>
    <p>
      These are the samples TulipFarm shows on its empty pages. Data, avatars,
      and file glyphs here are sample adapters; the package only draws the
      frame, rows, and placeholders.
    </p>
    <StateSampleGallery client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Lists and tables</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Table with column sizes"
      code={`<SampleTable
  columns={[
    { label: "Workflow", size: "wide" },
    { label: "Trigger" },
    { label: "Status", size: "narrow" },
  ]}
  rows={[
    [
      <><SampleMark tone="green" /><SampleText tone="strong">Approve large discounts</SampleText></>,
      <SampleText tone="muted">New quote</SampleText>,
      <Badge variant="success">Active</Badge>,
    ],
  ]}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>SampleList</code> takes <code>items</code>. Each item has a <code
        >title</code
      > and optional <code>detail</code>, <code>leading</code>, and <code
        >trailing</code
      > content. Rows are at least 56px tall.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>SampleTable</code> takes <code>columns</code> and <code>rows</code>.
      A column <code>size</code> is <code>"wide"</code> (1.6 shares), <code
        >"default"</code
      > (1 share), or <code>"narrow"</code> (a fixed 96px). Each row starts with a
      decorative checkbox. Long text truncates with an ellipsis.
    </p>
    <StateSampleWindows client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Parts</h2>
    <p>
      For <code>SampleText</code>, <code>tone</code> is <code>"default"</code>, <code
        >"strong"</code
      >, <code>"muted"</code>, <code>"link"</code>, or <code>"mono"</code>. A <code
        >SampleMark</code
      > is a colored square. Its <code>tone</code> is red, orange, green, blue, violet,
      or teal, and its <code>size</code> is <code>"sm"</code> (14px) or <code
        >"md"</code
      > (28px). A <code>SampleBar</code> stands in for a value. Its <code
        >width</code
      > is <code>"sm"</code>, <code>"md"</code>, or <code>"lg"</code>. A <code
        >SampleIconTile</code
      > puts an icon in a 28px tile.
    </p>
    <StateSampleParts client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Samples are pictures, not controls. Nothing in them can be focused. Marks,
      bars, icon tiles, checkboxes, and trail separators are hidden from
      assistive technology. Inside a State Panel the whole sample is hidden and
      inert, so screen readers hear only the panel text.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Lines use <code>--sprout-line</code>, text uses <code>--sprout-text</code> and
      <code>--sprout-muted</code>, links use <code>--sprout-info</code>, and
      bars use <code>--sprout-active</code>. Mark gradients have light and dark
      values set by the component.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
